WEBVTT

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.570
You!

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.630
Chihiro.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.590
<i>Yuri. Did he beat you?</i>

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.810
Koume-san, let's retreat.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.100
But we haven't—

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.250
There's something wrong with this mission.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.280
Fine.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:48.100
Wait!

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.230
Stop, Haru!

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.320
Don't chase them too far.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.080
But...

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.880
I'm worried about Yuri. Let's go.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.210
It's all because of your mother.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.980
Today's Dark Destiny Will Hang Over the Future

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.290
Chihiro.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.210
Chihiro, what happened after that light?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.710
I was cut off from your Arcana.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.670
I couldn't move.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:22.680
Hey, Chihiro!

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.180
Hey. Hey!

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.920
Sorry, but could you leave
me alone for a while?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.810
But Chihiro...

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:33.980
Don't make me say it again.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:35.810
Leave me alone.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:42.180
It's true! There was another.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.830
You were just dizzy.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:47.870
He summoned a monster from a weird pattern.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:51.460
They shouldn't be able to summon
monsters in areas without humans.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.710
Was it that boy with the hairband?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.700
Huh? That was a girl.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:04.220
Koetetsu-kun fought against
someone from the Guardian State.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.820
Guardian...

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:07.220
What is that?

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.800
The Guardian State.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.980
It's an organization that's
existed since ancient times.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:16.980
They've been protecting Japan since
long before this country was formed.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.170
Are they enemies?

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.990
I suppose they are.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:26.560
Come to think of it, Chihiro,
you disappeared during the battle.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.000
The guy with sunglasses
didn't seem to know either,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.750
but what happened when that light went off?

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.220
I don't know, either.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.810
By the time I came to, I was...

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.800
Even though you beat up bandanna boy?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.260
So you lost some time.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.940
Hey, I'm a busy man!

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:54.640
Quit asking me to show up
for every little thing!

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.150
Our information's being leaked to the enemy.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.190
A spy?

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.770
They're trying to kill all of us. There's no way.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.190
Then was the ambush a coincidence?

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.290
Even the Guardian State's involved now, right?

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.460
They know everything.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.920
Wouldn't that make you the prime suspect,
since you refused to participate in the mission?

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.920
I have nothing to gain
from selling you all out.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:27.680
There's no point in speculating.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.010
Let's think of how we'll handle
it during our next move.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:36.310
No one would walk out into the open if
they know they're going to get stabbed.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:39.330
We're not changing the plan.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.610
Wait.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.690
Speculation aside,

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.200
it <i>is</i> true that they were waiting in ambush.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.650
Are you scared?

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:49.660
I'm just saying it's dangerous to be hasty.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.410
I don't want to die yet.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:57.300
Our goal is to destroy Tokyo
as quickly as possible!

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.170
You understand that, don't you?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.410
It's all because of your mother.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.150
Are you feeling okay?

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.270
The mission's been shelved for now.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.130
Now's a good time for you to rest.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:30.950
Did something happen?

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:31.910
No.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.170
Someone told me

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.190
it's all because of my mother.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.550
Your mother?

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:49.490
I don't know.

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:51.550
But somehow, I can't stop thinking about it.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.280
About your mother?

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:58.160
I'd never thought about it
before, but her words...

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.500
Chihiro-kun?

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:06.210
I don't have any memories of my childhood.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.520
I don't remember my mother's face.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:11.660
If that's true,

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:15.660
then I know more about you than you do.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.630
Do you know something?

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.140
I can't believe you don't know your own mother,

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:26.880
given what a big story it was.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.960
Do you remember the explosion that
happened over ten years ago?

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:35.340
at the AVAL Science
Foundation research facility?

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.920
Yeah.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.690
His mother was responsible for the incident.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:46.940
But the nature of their research
was never made public.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.960
The individual responsible was missing.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:52.200
What do you mean?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.710
They never found a body.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:58.110
According to the announcement, she was missing.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.560
Missing?

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:04.330
Maybe someone took her out.

00:08:05.970 --> 00:08:08.350
Maybe you remember.

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:12.170
Didn't you kill your parents?

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.340
Kakihara-san, what are you—

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.280
Be honest. It bothers you, doesn't it?

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:22.370
Maybe if I tell you about how you stabbed
your dad, you'll remember your mom.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.840
That's enough!

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:28.260
Missing persons, amnesia...
How awfully convenient for you.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:42.500
You sure are tireless.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.460
Nothing's gonna change even if
you hang around here all the time.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:49.200
Are you studying?

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.420
At this rate, you won't get into college.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:55.320
I <i>am</i> a college student, though.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.790
Really? I thought you already failed once.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.530
You're really mean.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:07.130
I'll let you know if anything
happens. Get some rest.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:09.690
I've been telling him the same thing.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.190
If you can't recall, remember.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:18.450
I'll tell you what you wanna know,
so why not see it for yourself?

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.270
You're Kamina Chihiro-kun.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:33.280
Detective.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.300
Hey! We meet again.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.720
You're that girl!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.120
Time out!

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:40.600
Like I said, that was just a mix-up!

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:44.470
Well, you almost made a liar out of me.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:47.480
Are you sure that was my fault?

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.440
You're of the Heroic Lineage, too.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:55.480
I'm Kurokami Marie of the Guardian State.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.190
And this is...

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.450
Manazuru Tsubaki.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.290
The Guardian State...

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:08.060
Relax. We're not planning on
fighting you right now.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:10.380
What do you want, then?

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:15.550
Do you know about the murders
being committed around here lately?

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:17.470
A little.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:22.970
The victims were all slaughtered
as though by wild beasts.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.440
You think we did it?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.730
No, that's implausible.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:32.990
We're already pursuing another suspect.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.390
Another suspect?

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:36.220
His name is Aoi Jun.

00:10:37.270 --> 00:10:40.740
If you're of the Heroic Lineage,
you must've fought him before.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.810
He wears a blue jacket and sunglasses.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:45.750
Sound familiar?

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:51.000
Where is he?! Tell me!

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:55.230
That's what we're asking.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.340
Don't, Kotetsu.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.760
S-Sorry. I couldn't help myself.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:04.800
It doesn't seem like you know anything.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:07.480
Wait!

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.910
I'll help you look for him!

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:13.550
Please let me help you!

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:15.270
You?

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:18.030
I'll never forgive him!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.570
Sounds fun. Let's bring him along!

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.790
You look after him.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.410
Okay.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:29.910
Fine.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.150
Thank you!

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.660
Let's go, Chihiro-san.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.060
Sorry.

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:37.560
This didn't work, either.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:45.470
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:13:47.030 --> 00:13:48.080
You're—

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:48.880
I know.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.660
But there's no time.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:57.600
Inuki...

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:34.720
You're alone today?

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.940
Yeah.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.550
You show up every day.

00:14:38.990 --> 00:14:43.150
It's my fault this happened to Ikuro.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.230
Don't blame yourself.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:48.620
I don't think he would blame you.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:52.220
It'd be better if he did.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.100
His numbers have stabilized.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:15:00.280
He's responding well to the treatment.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:07.810
I discovered a component in the Red Mist
that alleviates Arcana syndrome.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:09.910
You did?

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:13.010
We can't rely on outsiders.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:17.400
It's not ready yet, but if I'm able
to fabricate higher purity matter,

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.020
then I'll be able to save
patients like Ikuro-kun.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:22.450
Really?

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:26.440
Yeah. It's because I kept
searching for an answer.

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:29.510
We need to do everything we can.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:35.080
I don't want to have any regrets.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:39.290
I can't just let them die.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.950
Chihiro-kun?

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.820
Did you go to the research lab?

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:53.080
I can only destroy.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:57.070
When I seek salvation, only despair remains.

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:59.610
That's the path Dux created.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.820
But she's right.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:06.400
We've been drawn to the church by fate,

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:11.570
but I think it's wrong to sacrifice
someone to save another.

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:15.900
We should be saving
everyone who lives in Tokyo.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:20.540
I would if I could.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.840
We can.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:24.780
Talk is easy.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.850
It's easy to say that and run.

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.130
You're not a child, though.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.800
Tell me what you think.

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:41.170
I want to be forgiven.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.040
I want to escape from despair.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.760
I don't want to kill and destroy.

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:49.970
Then why?

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.700
Because there's no salvation
for me no matter where I go.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:02.690
It's okay. I came up with a treatment.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.040
No matter how crazy,
as long as you don't give up,

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.460
you'll always find a solution.

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:13.490
Do you think I can do it?

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:15.840
If you want to.

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:20.720
I'll help you. Let's work together.

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.220
Okay.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:27.190
I'm glad to hear you say that.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.500
Thank you, Doctor.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.940
You don't need to call me that.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:34.370
Call me by my name.

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:36.160
Okay, Doctor.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:41.240
We haven't found any clues, much less Aoi Jun.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.660
Based on the victims' wounds,

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:47.550
the murders were all committed
by the same individual.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:48.750
Yeah.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:53.270
Which means a familiar is
committing murders here in Tokyo

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.630
without anyone noticing.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:58.030
Do you think that's possible?

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.000
No.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:07.390
Maybe we're actually pursuing something else.

00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:32.530
Hello, Akaya Research Lab.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.880
Doctor! I mean, is Inuki-san there?!

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.730
What's gotten into you?

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:37.770
Put him on the phone!

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.470
I don't get it.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.330
Hey, you okay?!

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.520
Inuki...

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:01.740
<i>I won't let any more people die!</i>

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:35.140
<i>Where did you go, Doctor?</i>

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:37.400
Doctor, over here!

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:40.620
<i>"Doctor"?</i>

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.170
It's him.

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:14.340
He can't have gone far.

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:15.380
We can still—

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:20.570
D-Den...

00:20:28.250 --> 00:20:29.160
Tsubaki-chan!

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:45.860
Tsubaki-chan!

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:49.820
Don't worry about me.

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.310
Hurry up and go after him...

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.310
I can't just leave you!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.570
Kotecchan...
